WEBVTT

00:03:28.156 --> 00:03:30.756
Like, I literally -- sorry to go on
with this question,

00:03:30.796 --> 00:03:35.996
but I literally have sitting taped up
in front of me in my office right now ...

00:03:37.836 --> 00:03:40.996
A quotation from the poet
Jalāl al-Dīn Rūmī,

00:03:41.036 --> 00:03:43.036
who was a Sufi poet,

00:03:43.076 --> 00:03:45.316
and I'm going to quote it for you,

00:03:45.356 --> 00:03:49.076
but I'm just going to set
the context of the poem.

00:03:49.596 --> 00:03:50.876
It's basically ...

00:03:51.716 --> 00:03:55.356
It’s about a man who is praying to Allah,

00:03:55.396 --> 00:03:58.796
and a cynical person
comes along and asks him,

00:03:58.836 --> 00:04:00.036
"Why are you praying?